Q: Knowledge Base acceptable input variable A: <p>Alright, after you mentioned needing the expected format i went and checked the <a href="https://docs.dify.ai/en/use-dify/knowledge/knowledge-pipeline/knowledge-pipeline-orchestration" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Dify</a> docs and found that the Knowledge Base node expects each chunk like this</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;content&quot;: &quot;your text here&quot;,
  &quot;metadata&quot;: {}
}
</code></pre>
<p>your structure is actually close, the problem is you are wrapping everything inside a chunks key and the node expects the array directly as the output variable, not nested inside an object.</p>
<p>so in your code node just return the array direct instead of <code>{ &quot;chunks&quot;:[] }</code> and declare your outputs as <code>Array[Object]</code> pointing to the array.</p>
<p>Let me know if it works :)</p>

Q: JOIN the same table to a parent table twice by relating to different columns using CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>Heres how I do it using aliases. You can format it your way too.</p>

<pre><code> $this-&gt;db-&gt;select('tb1.*,tb2.*,u.*');
 $this-&gt;db-&gt;join('table1name tb1','tb1.id = u.tb1_id');
 $this-&gt;db-&gt;join('table2name tb2','tb2.id = u.tb2_id');
 $this-&gt;db-&gt;order_by('u.id_key','DESC');
 $result = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('User u')-&gt;result();
</code></pre>

<p>If you want to alter between left and right join just add 'left' or 'right' to the join function.</p>

<pre><code> $this-&gt;db-&gt;join('table1name pr1','pr1.id = u.tb1_id','right');
 $this-&gt;db-&gt;join('table2name tb2','tb2.id = u.tb2_id','right');
</code></pre>

<p>This would preference your user table.</p>

